 "title": "The Fano plane is the only uniform law that contradicts itself",
 "subject": "Which point- and line-transitive knot laws with uniform signs are unsatisfiable",
 "conclusion": "A simple cubic triple system whose symmetries are transitive on its points and on its lines has a brace for its incidence graph, so by Seymour's dictionary and McCuaig's theorem the Fano plane is its only non-2-colourable case. Since non-constant uniform signs are satisfied by the all-zero assignment, the Fano plane is the only uniform knot law that contradicts itself.",
